00:09:26,120 --> 00:09:26,960
It sure is.

285
00:09:27,280 --> 00:09:28,560
The water looks so nice.

286
00:09:29,280 --> 00:09:30,480
Anchor the boat for a little while.

287
00:09:30,840 --> 00:09:31,700
I'm going to take a dip.

288
00:09:36,160 --> 00:09:37,920
Why are you doggy paddling?

289
00:09:38,320 --> 00:09:39,300
I taught you how to swim.

290
00:09:39,740 --> 00:09:41,160
Do your breaststroke.

291
00:09:41,580 --> 00:09:42,720
I get too tired.

292
00:09:43,560 --> 00:09:44,960
I'll just backstroke.

293
00:09:45,260 --> 00:09:45,540
It's easier.

294
00:09:47,440 --> 00:09:48,800
Try kicking your legs more.

295
00:09:49,900 --> 00:09:50,300
That's good.

296
00:09:51,140 --> 00:09:51,840
Don't go out too far.

297
00:09:52,460 --> 00:09:53,440
It's fine.

298
00:09:54,040 --> 00:09:54,740
Jump in.

299
00:09:55,600 --> 00:09:58,600
Cathy, get back here.

300
00:09:58,660 --> 00:09:59,200
I see a shark.

301
00:09:59,600 --> 00:10:00,600
Help me!

302
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:01,600
Help!

303
00:10:01,600 --> 00:10:02,600
Bring the boat closer.

304
00:10:02,600 --> 00:10:03,600
The shark is coming straight towards me.

305
00:10:03,600 --> 00:10:04,600
It's right under you.

306
00:10:04,600 --> 00:10:05,600
Cathy!

307
00:10:13,710 --> 00:10:30,530
All right, well, Marco, I was telling you that I used to spend every summer on the lake and my family had a really small house on a small island and my cousins had another small house on another small island.

308
00:10:31,680 --> 00:10:39,390
So our families are really close and we used to go to one house for dinner one night and the other house to dinner the next night.

309
00:10:40,160 --> 00:10:43,850
So everyone was over at my cousin's house except for my grandfather.

310
00:10:45,840 --> 00:10:53,000
And so he was thinking, okay, it's late, maybe I better go pick up my wife and see what's going on.

311
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:54,190
So he goes into the boat.

312
00:10:55,160 --> 00:10:55,410
It's dark.

313
00:10:56,160 --> 00:10:57,160
Okay.

314
00:10:57,160 --> 00:10:57,570
There's no light on the boat.

315
00:10:58,660 --> 00:11:07,420
He's driving straight towards the island when suddenly my cousin in his boat drives directly into my grandfather.

316
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:08,680
So they crashed.

317
00:11:09,200 --> 00:11:09,360
They crashed.

318
00:11:10,200 --> 00:11:11,160
Two boats crashed in the lake.

319
00:11:11,680 --> 00:11:14,800
And then my grandfather's boat flipped over.

320
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:17,320
It turned upside down.

321
00:11:17,320 --> 00:11:18,280
And he fell in the water.

322
00:11:19,280 --> 00:11:19,960
But he was okay, right?

323
00:11:20,280 --> 00:11:21,280
Yeah, he was okay.

324
00:11:21,280 --> 00:11:22,360
But you know what?

325
00:11:22,360 --> 00:11:25,080
He was really angry about this.

326
00:11:25,080 --> 00:11:25,380
And the boat?

327
00:11:26,080 --> 00:11:30,570
The boat stayed in the water and the engine fell down to the bottom.

328
00:11:31,560 --> 00:11:34,010
So we had to go the next morning to get the boat.

329
00:11:34,120 --> 00:11:40,190
And we actually had to hire some scuba divers to go to the bottom of the lake to get the engine.

330
00:11:41,080 --> 00:11:42,080
Wow.

331
00:11:42,080 --> 00:11:43,080
Yeah.

332
00:11:43,080 --> 00:11:44,560
I imagine your grandpa was pretty angry.

333
00:11:44,560 --> 00:11:45,560
Yeah.

334
00:11:45,560 --> 00:11:46,070
He tells the story.

335
00:11:46,560 --> 00:11:47,310
Every year.

336
00:11:47,560 --> 00:11:48,210
Yeah, exactly.

337
00:11:49,370 --> 00:11:50,130
But you know what?

338
00:11:50,170 --> 00:11:55,030
I've got a million of these crazy lake stories because my family.

339
00:11:55,400 --> 00:11:55,950
It always happens.

340
00:11:56,400 --> 00:11:57,400
Yeah.

341
00:11:57,890 --> 00:11:58,370
All right, guys.

342
00:11:58,590 --> 00:12:02,710
Well, do you have any crazy stories or any stories related to boats or to swimming?

343
00:12:03,080 --> 00:12:03,650
Or to shark attacks?

344
00:12:04,080 --> 00:12:04,710
Or shark attacks?

345
00:12:05,080 --> 00:12:06,080
Yeah.

346
00:12:06,080 --> 00:12:08,280
So come to our website, EnglishPod.com.

347
00:12:08,280 --> 00:12:08,750
Leave your stories.

348
00:12:09,280 --> 00:12:09,630
Share with us.

349
00:12:10,280 --> 00:12:13,850
And also, if you have any doubts or questions, Erica and I are always there to answer.

350
00:12:14,170 --> 00:12:15,850
Well, we're out of time for this lesson.

351
00:12:16,240 --> 00:12:26,080
But until next time, goodbye.
